(Pool-vs-FIXED-binding disjointness - FUZZER_DEFECTS.md Defect 16. Every
 row above checks two STATIC lists for a shared word. A FIXED binding is
 not a list: it is a name a leaf expects to find ALREADY BOUND once the
 manifest is built - gen_scratch_flag (gen_files.vox, gen_buffers.vox -
 the scratch directory the harness supplies) and gen_reader_name /
 gen_grid_sink_name (gen_misc.vox, gen_flow.vox - the flag-reader and
 grid-sink calls). Each is drawn once per program and threaded by
 variable rather than re-drawn, so there is no second list to diff it
 against; the only way to prove the binding held is to build the
 manifest, many times, and check what it actually produced.

 'gen program' builds the manifest and argv before it draws a single
 statement, so a small budget is enough - these checks only read state
 set in that first half. Every count below must read 0.)

To 'count number equal to' with a list called 'the numbers' and a number called target.
    a number called 'the hits' is 0.
    a number called 'how many' is 'the numbers's length.
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'how many',
        a number called 'the candidate' is element 'the position' of 'the numbers',
        If 'the candidate' is target then,
            Set 'the hits' to 'the hits' add 1.
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    Return a number, 'the hits'.

(The written name of whichever flag holds role 1, "" if none does - used
 only after 'role ones' below has already confirmed there is exactly
 one, so ambiguity here cannot hide a defect.)

To 'the scratch role written name'.
    a number called 'how many flags' is gen_flag_role's length.
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    a text called 'the found name' is "".
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'how many flags',
        a number called 'the role' is element 'the position' of gen_flag_role,
        If 'the role' is 1 then,
            Set 'the found name' to element 'the position' of gen_flag_written_names.
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    Return a text, 'the found name'.

a number called 'fixed binding trial' is 0.
a number called 'file io trials' is 0.
a number called 'unbound scratch flag' is 0.
a number called 'scratch role miscount' is 0.
a number called 'scratch role name mismatch' is 0.
a number called 'scratch flag picked for argv stress' is 0.
a number called 'reader equals sink' is 0.
a number called 'reader in ordinary functions' is 0.
a number called 'sink in ordinary functions' is 0.
a number called 'reader in flag names' is 0.
a number called 'sink in flag names' is 0.
While 'fixed binding trial' is less than 1000,
    'gen program' of 'fixed binding trial' and 3,
    a number called 'role ones' is 'count number equal to' of gen_flag_role and 1,
    (Flat, single-statement Ifs throughout this body on purpose - note
     6b's own hazard: a multi-statement If closed with one period early
     leaves a later If nested inside it, and if that later If's condition
     is false on trial 0 (deterministic per seed), the loop's own
     increment below can end up skipped every single time, which is an
     infinite loop, not a wrong count. Every check here repeats its
     guard condition instead of nesting under one.)
    If gen_does_file_io then, Set 'file io trials' to 'file io trials' add 1.
    If gen_does_file_io is false and 'role ones' is not 0 then, Set 'scratch role miscount' to 'scratch role miscount' add 1.
    If gen_does_file_io and gen_scratch_flag is empty then, Set 'unbound scratch flag' to 'unbound scratch flag' add 1.
    If gen_does_file_io and 'role ones' is not 1 then, Set 'scratch role miscount' to 'scratch role miscount' add 1.
    a text called 'the scratch written name' is 'the scratch role written name',
    If gen_does_file_io and 'the scratch written name' is not gen_scratch_flag then, Set 'scratch role name mismatch' to 'scratch role name mismatch' add 1.
    a number called 'the text flag role' is 0,
    If gen_text_flag is not 0 then, Set 'the text flag role' to element gen_text_flag of gen_flag_role.
    If 'the text flag role' is 1 then, Set 'scratch flag picked for argv stress' to 'scratch flag picked for argv stress' add 1.
    a number called 'the number flag role' is 0,
    If gen_number_flag is not 0 then, Set 'the number flag role' to element gen_number_flag of gen_flag_role.
    If 'the number flag role' is 1 then, Set 'scratch flag picked for argv stress' to 'scratch flag picked for argv stress' add 1.
    a number called 'the boolean flag role' is 0,
    If gen_boolean_flag is not 0 then, Set 'the boolean flag role' to element gen_boolean_flag of gen_flag_role.
    If 'the boolean flag role' is 1 then, Set 'scratch flag picked for argv stress' to 'scratch flag picked for argv stress' add 1.
    If gen_reader_name is gen_grid_sink_name then, Set 'reader equals sink' to 'reader equals sink' add 1.
    a number called 'reader hits' is 'times a pool holds' of gen_function_written_names and gen_reader_name,
    If 'reader hits' is not 0 then, Set 'reader in ordinary functions' to 'reader in ordinary functions' add 1.
    a number called 'sink hits' is 'times a pool holds' of gen_function_written_names and gen_grid_sink_name,
    If 'sink hits' is not 0 then, Set 'sink in ordinary functions' to 'sink in ordinary functions' add 1.
    a number called 'reader flag hits' is 'times a pool holds' of gen_flag_written_names and gen_reader_name,
    If 'reader flag hits' is not 0 then, Set 'reader in flag names' to 'reader in flag names' add 1.
    a number called 'sink flag hits' is 'times a pool holds' of gen_flag_written_names and gen_grid_sink_name,
    If 'sink flag hits' is not 0 then, Set 'sink in flag names' to 'sink in flag names' add 1.
    Set 'fixed binding trial' to 'fixed binding trial' add 1.
Print "fixed-binding trials: {'fixed binding trial'} file-io={'file io trials'}".
Print "scratch flag unbound while file-io: {'unbound scratch flag'}".
Print "scratch role count wrong: {'scratch role miscount'}".
Print "scratch role written name mismatch: {'scratch role name mismatch'}".
Print "scratch flag picked for argv stress: {'scratch flag picked for argv stress'}".
Print "reader name equals grid sink name: {'reader equals sink'}".
Print "reader name in ordinary functions: {'reader in ordinary functions'}".
Print "grid sink name in ordinary functions: {'sink in ordinary functions'}".
