Print "grid sink name in flag names: {'sink in flag names'}".

(No prelude word may CONTAIN one of tests/200_never_emitted.vox's banned
 needles. That guard scans generated source for the substring, so a name
 that merely embeds one trips it: "amount" contains "mount" and did,
 failing the safety guard at seed 2 the first time these pools grew.
 200 catches it across a 2000-program sweep; this catches it in the one
 place it can be fixed, and says which word.)

To 'the word holds' with a text called 'the word' and a text called needle.
    a buffer called 'the word bytes' is "{'the word'}".
    a buffer called 'the needle bytes' is "{needle}".
    a number called 'how long' is 'the word bytes's size.
    a number called 'how long a needle' is 'the needle bytes's size.
    a number called 'the start' is 1.
    a boolean called 'it is here' is false.
    While 'the start' is less than or equal to 'how long',
        a boolean called 'this one matches' is 'the word matches at' of 'the word bytes' and 'the start' and 'the needle bytes' and 'how long a needle' and 'how long',
        If 'this one matches' then,
            Set 'it is here' to true.
        Set 'the start' to 'the start' add 1.
    Return a boolean, 'it is here'.

To 'the word matches at' with a buffer called 'the word bytes' and a number called 'the start' and a buffer called 'the needle bytes' and a number called 'how long a needle' and a number called 'how long'.
    a number called 'the end' is 'the start' add 'how long a needle' minus 1.
    If 'the end' is greater than 'how long' then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the step' is 0.
    a boolean called 'still matching' is true.
    While 'the step' is less than 'how long a needle',
        a number called 'the word position' is 'the start' add 'the step',
        a number called 'the needle position' is 'the step' add 1,
        a number called 'the word byte' is byte 'the word position' of 'the word bytes',
        a number called 'the needle byte' is byte 'the needle position' of 'the needle bytes',
        If 'the word byte' is not 'the needle byte' then,
            Set 'still matching' to false.
        Set 'the step' to 'the step' add 1.
    Return a boolean, 'still matching'.

To 'banned needles in' with a list called 'the pool'.
    a list called 'the needles' is ["shutdown", "poweroff", "reboot", "restart", "halt", "mount", "pivot", "device node"].
    a number called 'the hits' is 0.
    a number called 'how many words' is 'the pool's length.
    a number called 'how many needles' is 'the needles's length.
    a number called 'the word position' is 1.
    While 'the word position' is less than or equal to 'how many words',
        a text called 'the word' is element 'the word position' of 'the pool',
        a number called 'these hits' is 'banned needles in one' of 'the word' and 'the needles' and 'how many needles',
        Set 'the hits' to 'the hits' add 'these hits',
        Set 'the word position' to 'the word position' add 1.
    Return a number, 'the hits'.

To 'banned needles in one' with a text called 'the word' and a list called 'the needles' and a number called 'how many needles'.
    a number called 'the hits' is 0.
    a number called 'the needle position' is 1.
    While 'the needle position' is less than or equal to 'how many needles',
        a text called needle is element 'the needle position' of 'the needles',
        a boolean called 'it is here' is 'the word holds' of 'the word' and needle,
        If 'it is here' then,
            Set 'the hits' to 'the hits' add 1.
        Set 'the needle position' to 'the needle position' add 1.
    Return a number, 'the hits'.

Print "banned needles in types: {'banned needles in' of gen_type_words}".
Print "banned needles in fields: {'banned needles in' of gen_field_words}".
Print "banned needles in makers: {'banned needles in' of gen_maker_words}".
Print "banned needles in receivers: {'banned needles in' of gen_receiver_words}".
Print "banned needles in functions: {'banned needles in' of gen_function_words}".
Print "banned needles in parameters: {'banned needles in' of gen_parameter_words}".
Print "banned needles in flags: {'banned needles in' of gen_flag_words}".
Print "banned needles in buffers: {'banned needles in' of gen_buffer_words}".
Print "banned needles in value nouns: {'banned needles in' of 'the value nouns'}".
Print "banned needles in value verbs: {'banned needles in' of 'the value verbs'}".
Print "banned needles in environment: {'banned needles in' of gen_environment_words}".
Print "banned needles in loop words: {'banned needles in' of gen_environment_loop_words}".
Print "banned needles in spoken words: {'banned needles in' of gen_environment_spoken_words}".

(G1 / FUZZER_DEFECTS.md defect 14: a float drawn for a leaf that declares
 it as quoted text and asserts it against the bare literal must
 round-trip - the two parse routes agree only while the payload has at
 most 17 significant digits (the IEEE-754 round-trip bound). Beyond 18
 the text route takes the nearest double of the prefix and the literal
 route the nearest double of the whole, one ulp apart, and the leaf's
 cross-route assertion becomes unwinnable. 'gen round trippable float'
 is the draw that clamps to 17; this counts the significant digits in a
 thousand of its draws and pins the max, so a change that lets a
 >17-digit payload through fails here instead of in a campaign.)

To 'significant digits in' with a text called 'the float text'.
    a buffer called 'the bytes' is "{'the float text'}".
    a number called 'the size' is 'the bytes's size.
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    a number called 'the count' is 0.
    a boolean called 'seen nonzero' is false.
    (Flattened to single-statement Ifs on purpose: a nested If would
     close on its own period and leave the position increment inside the
     outer clause, so a decimal point - byte 46 - would skip the
     increment and loop forever. 46 is the decimal point, 48 is '0';
     leading zeros before the first nonzero digit are not significant,
     and from the first nonzero on every digit counts.)
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'the size',
        a number called 'the byte' is byte 'the position' of 'the bytes',
        If 'the byte' is not 46 and 'the byte' is not 48 then, Set 'seen nonzero' to true.
        If 'seen nonzero' and 'the byte' is not 46 then, Set 'the count' to 'the count' add 1.
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    Return a number, 'the count'.

'rng seed' of 990321.
a number called 'the float draw count' is 0.
a number called 'the most significant digits' is 0.
a number called 'too wide' is 0.
While 'the float draw count' is less than 1000,
    a text called 'a drawn float' is 'gen round trippable float',
    a number called 'its significant digits' is 'significant digits in' of 'a drawn float',
    If 'its significant digits' is greater than 'the most significant digits' then,
        Set 'the most significant digits' to 'its significant digits'.
    If 'its significant digits' is greater than 17 then,
        Set 'too wide' to 'too wide' add 1.
    Set 'the float draw count' to 'the float draw count' add 1.
Print "round-trip float: max-sig-digits={'the most significant digits'} too-wide={'too wide'} (max<=17 and too-wide=0 means every drawn literal round-trips through both parse routes)".

(FUZZER_DEFECTS.md Defect 20: 'gen leaf thing equality' (gen_things.vox)
 forces two thing instances' shared field apart by drawing two literals
 and redrawing the second one while it numerically equals the first -
 not while either equals a hardcoded 0, and not by comparing the
 literals' TEXT. A signed leading-zero literal like "-00008" is
 textually distinct from "-8" while numerically identical - exactly the
 collision that turned a thing's own declared field default ("depth"
 defaults to -8) into a false THG2-09 finding at seed 20260856: the old
 guard only redrew a literal that parsed to 0, so a redraw landing on
 any OTHER nonzero default slipped through untouched.

 This does not drive the leaf itself - that needs a thing/field
 manifest, which the targeted campaign re-probe (seed 20260856,
 `./build/vox-fuzz gen --seed 20260856 --count 1 --layout plain`, 0
 findings) and the rest of test.sh already exercise end to end. It pins
 the mechanism the fix depends on, at the same grain as the round-trip
 float check above: draw 'literal integer' - the exact routine the leaf
 calls - many times, counting how often two independent draws collide on
 the same NUMBER despite different TEXT (proving the collision is a real
 rate in this literal space, not a hypothetical), then runs the fix's
 own redraw loop and confirms it always leaves the pair numerically
 distinct. A regression that goes back to comparing text, or back to
 comparing against a hardcoded 0, fails here before it ever reaches a
 campaign.)

'rng seed' of 20260856.
a number called 'the equality trial' is 0.
a number called 'the same-number collisions' is 0.
a number called 'the same-number different-text collisions' is 0.
a number called 'the redraws spent' is 0.
a number called 'the most redraws in one trial' is 0.
a number called 'the trials that ended equal' is 0.
While 'the equality trial' is less than 5000,
    a text called 'the first literal' is 'literal integer',
    a number called 'the first value' is 'the first literal' as a number,
    a text called 'the second literal' is 'literal integer',
    a number called 'the second value' is 'the second literal' as a number,
    If 'the second value' is 'the first value' then,
        Set 'the same-number collisions' to 'the same-number collisions' add 1.
    If 'the second value' is 'the first value' and 'the second literal' is not 'the first literal' then,
        Set 'the same-number different-text collisions' to 'the same-number different-text collisions' add 1.
    a number called 'the redraws this trial' is 0,
    While 'the second value' is 'the first value',
        Set 'the second literal' to 'literal integer',
        Set 'the second value' to 'the second literal' as a number,
        Set 'the redraws this trial' to 'the redraws this trial' add 1.
    If 'the redraws this trial' is greater than 'the most redraws in one trial' then,
        Set 'the most redraws in one trial' to 'the redraws this trial'.
    Set 'the redraws spent' to 'the redraws spent' add 'the redraws this trial',
    If 'the second value' is 'the first value' then,
        Set 'the trials that ended equal' to 'the trials that ended equal' add 1.
    Set 'the equality trial' to 'the equality trial' add 1.
Print "thing-equality literal pairs: {'the equality trial'} same-number-collisions={'the same-number collisions'} same-number-different-text={'the same-number different-text collisions'} redraws-spent={'the redraws spent'} max-redraws-one-trial={'the most redraws in one trial'} ended-equal={'the trials that ended equal'} (ended-equal must be 0 - that is the redraw loop's whole job)".
